TITLE: Reaction and safe state

[SSR]
UID: SSR-001
TITLE: Reaction decided in one place
FINDINGS: F1
STAGE: 1
ASIL: B
STATUS: implemented
VERIFICATION: test, review
REVIEW_STATUS: inspected
CODE: >>>
ecu/safety/safeSupervisor/src/safeSupervisor/SafeSupervisor.cpp :: SafeSupervisor::handle
<<<
NOTE: >>>
Realisation: events are raised on monitors of the supervisor (trigger, check, hit); the single place of (c) is
SafeSupervisor::handle(). Clause (c) is verified by review. SYS-117 added SD to (b): an event of the closed list
whose project mapping names safe-output groups gets SD instead of its fail-safe reaction, decided in handle()
as well (SSR-087).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ASG-06
  ROLE: DerivedFrom

[CLAUSE]
UID: SSR-001(a)
STATEMENT: >>>
Every safety mechanism of the base software shall report a detected fault only as an event to the safe
supervisor, optionally with one context word, and shall not choose a reaction itself.
<<<
VERIFICATION: test
TESTS: kernel-fault-reaction, kernel-fault-reaction-mutations, no-heap-operator-delete
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSR-001

[CLAUSE]
UID: SSR-001(b)
STATEMENT: >>>
The safe supervisor shall assign to every event it defines exactly one reaction out of S3 (report and
continue), SD (degraded, only as SSR-087 allows), S1, S1 held and S1 + S2.
<<<
VERIFICATION: test
TESTS: safe-supervisor, safe-supervisor-bare, safe-supervisor-degraded, safety-reset-console, safety-reset-console-mutations, safe-console
REVIEW_STATUS: accepted
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSR-001

[CLAUSE]
UID: SSR-001(c)
STATEMENT: The reaction to an event shall be selected at exactly one place of the safe supervisor.
VERIFICATION: review
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSR-001

[SSR]
UID: SSR-002
TITLE: De-energise before every safety reset
STATEMENT: >>>
For every event whose reaction includes a software reset (S2), the safe supervisor shall complete S1 (every
entry of the safe outputs table, SSR-005, driven to its inactive level) before it requests the reset.
<<<
STAGE: 1
ASIL: B
STATUS: implemented
VERIFICATION: test
REVIEW_STATUS: inspected
CODE: >>>
ecu/safety/safeSupervisor/src/safeSupervisor/SafeSupervisor.cpp :: SafeSupervisor::handle
<<<
