Realisation: time-out SafeWatchdog::WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT_MS from modules.safeLifecycle.watchdog_timeout_ms (250 ms
in the demo); serviced through SafeWatchdog every SafetyManager::WATCHDOG_CYCLIC_COUNTER safety cycles
(derived by tools/nxconfig as floor(time-out / (3 x task period))); (d) by the watchdog warning interrupt.
partial - a slowed safety task below 31.25 ms per cycle is not detected by the watchdog (F9); since SYS-40 the
period check SSR-018 (SM-04) covers it against the same LPO clock. Since SYS-41 CS[INT] (the
warning interrupt that de-energises before the reset) is re-checked at every service (SSR-012, SSR-066,
test safe-watchdog); board check B6 of fmea.md section 8 (clear CS[INT] with the probe) is open.
<<<
