Realisation: event SAFETY_CYCLE_PERIOD_VIOLATION. SYS-40 (SM-04): LPTMR on the 1 kHz LPO clock; bound 14 ticks per
interval (an interval of 17 ms or more is
always reported, derived from the 10 ms period, CYCLE_LATENESS_MS = 2 ms and the LPO range of the data sheet),
window 8 cycles >= 68 ticks. Host verified with mutants (cycle-period-check, lptmr-cycle-timer, safety-cycle,
cycle-period-constants). partial - detection happens when the late cycle runs; a stall that ends before the
watchdog fires has no hardware deadline yet (T1b); board checks B4 and B7 of fmea.md section 8 are open; the
since SYS-25 period and lateness are project values (modules.safeLifecycle), the window is the derived service
interval.
<<<
