CODE: >>>
platforms/s32k1xx/port/safety/safeMemory/src/safeMemory/IntegrityEccHandler.cpp :: checkRamDoubleBitError
platforms/s32k1xx/port/safety/safeMemory/src/safeMemory/IntegrityEccHandler.cpp :: takeEccErrors
<<<
NOTE: >>>
SYS-41 (F11 closed, F15 closed by safe-memory-ecc): the reference manual (S32K1xx RM Rev. 13, 22.4) confirms
that ERM_SR0 records without the CR0 enables; takeEccErrors() reads ERM_SR0 once, keeps the RAM address and
clears exactly the flags it read before the report (no reset loop, no masking), the event carries the source
(bit 0 RAM channel 0, bit 1 RAM channel 1, bit 2 flash) - the completion is SSR-068. Coverage limit: memory
that is not read is not checked (no scrubbing, fmea.md SM-15). Board check B5 (ERM_SR0 after an injected
error and after a reset) is open; the behaviour no longer depends on it.
<<<
