UID: SSR-060
TITLE: Safe state verified by read-back
FINDINGS: G1
STAGE: 1
ASIL: B
STATUS: partial
VERIFICATION: test, board
REVIEW_STATUS: inspected
CODE: >>>
platforms/s32k1xx/port/safety/safeIo/src/safeIo/SafeIo.cpp :: readsBackSafe
platforms/s32k1xx/port/safety/safeIo/include/safeIo/SafeIoRegisters.h :: readbackAccepts
platforms/s32k1xx/port/safety/safeIo/src/registerList/SafeOutputReadbackList.cpp :: safeOutputReadbacks
tools/bswgen/bswgen.py :: collect_safe_outputs
<<<
NOTE: >>>
SYS-30 (2026-09-30). Realisation: the generator writes one read-back entry per entry of the safe outputs table
(NX_SAFE_OUTPUT_READBACKS: for a PWM group its software output control, CHnOC set and CHnOCV clear; for a
safe_off output the pin level PDIR of its port, the inactive level), defined in the register list library of
SafeIo; SafeIo::cyclic() reads them in every safety cycle while the latch of S1 is set and raises
LOCK_REGISTER_ERROR with context class SAFE_OUTPUT and the entry index for the first entry that does not show
the safe state (reaction S1 + S2: the reset puts the pins into their reset state), once until the next init().
With an active short selected (SYS-116, SSR-089) the short passes as well. SYS-138 (2026-09-30, decision K6 of
the safety review SYS-116/SYS-30): the read-back is one function of the family port that the safe supervisor uses
as well - in S1 held in every round of the hold loop before its walk, for the groups of SD in every safety cycle
before their walk, and in the S1 + S2 sequence before the reset (then without the console line); not confirmed:
LOCK_REGISTER_ERROR, S1 + S2. An entry whose clock is gated is not confirmed once SafeIo::init() has run (before
SYS-138 it was not judged). Host verified (safe-io, safe-supervisor-degraded, with mutants). Partial: not yet in
the hard fault and watchdog handlers and the halt deadman of the family port; nothing is judged before
SafeIo::init(); with the input of a pin disabled (a register fault SM-22 reports itself) its level reads 0;
board proof open (fmea.md B15, B16).
<<<
