SYS-44 (task T5): period modules.safeMemory.rom_check_period_ms (default 60000 ms, start to start); every pass
begins with a known-answer test (ROMCHECK_UNIT_FAILED); no pass starts while a flash write is open (every NvM
write is bracketed, FlashWriteBracket) or a flash command runs (FTFC FSTAT CCIF), a pass during which one began
is discarded, a due pass kept off for more than one period is reported (ROMCHECK_OVERDUE). The data flash
written by the NvM is suspended as well as the program flash. Host verified with 17 mutants; board B1/B9 open.
Known limit: with period 0 a write that never ends keeps the first pass off without a report.
<<<
