SYS-73 (iso26262-gap.md section 6 no. 18). Realisation: error injection module (EIM) per ERM channel of the
derivative (S32K14x: SRAM_L and SRAM_U; S32K11x: SRAM_U, double-bit case left out because the Cortex-M0+ takes
it as a hard fault), reserved words in the hot bss and the no-init RAM, called in main() after the reset-loop
limit; failure = INTEGRITY_EVENT_DMA_ECC_ERROR with context bit 3 (S1 + S2, after the configured number of such
resets S1 held by SSR-065). Host tests safe-memory-ecc-latent (both layouts) with 25 mutants, placement and
register-only window on the linked image (safe-memory-ecc-latent-elf). Board run open. The flash ECC has no
injection module; what can be tested without erasing or programming is in fmea.md SM-55.
<<<
